PRIVATE REFLECTION: {Most colleagues converge on {B2} as the unique forcing first move. Key shared reasoning: the C1-C2 black group has exactly two liberties (B1,B2); B2 places it in atari. Black's only non-immediate-loss reply is B1 (capturing the single stone at B2), after which the enlarged black group again has only two liberties and White can continue the atari sequence (A1 etc.) to capture regardless of replies. Surrounding White stones (C3/C4/D1/D2) prevent escape or extra eyes. Colleagues 2,3,4,5,7,8,9,10,12 give consistent variants of this. 

Disagreements: Colleague 6 claims B2 is suicide (false—B2 has liberty at B1 when played and is therefore legal) and proposes {B1} instead; this is refuted by the capture-sequence analysis above. Colleague 11 claims the whole black cluster has five liberties and no forcing line (incorrect liberty count for the isolated C1-C2 subgroup; the other black stones are separate groups). 

No other first move (A3,B1,etc.) appears in any argument as unconditionally forcing capture. Persistent open question for later rounds: exact continuation tree after Black's B1 reply—need to confirm White always answers without allowing ko or connection.}

